| 2026-07-21 | Guide v2.45: CLI **v0.144.6** (July 18) + **v0.145.0** (stable, July 21, promoted from the alpha line). **`/import`:** now migrates **Cursor** as well as Claude Code — settings, MCP servers, plugins, sessions, commands, project-scoped memories (see slash-command table). **Sessions:** experimental **paginated thread history** — efficient resume, search, persisted names, sub-agent support, memories (see Session Management). **Multi-agent:** **v2 stabilized as opt-in** with configurable sub-agent models, reasoning levels, concurrency, restored roles, improved agent navigation (see Multi-Agent). **Voice:** audio inputs and tool outputs (common local formats) + **streaming realtime V3 conversations** — realtime returns after its v0.140.0 removal (see TUI Enhancements). **Bedrock:** experimental login with custom endpoint + authentication support; **GPT-5.6 Sol is the default Bedrock model** (see Authentication, Available Models). **Models:** bundled GPT-5.4 selections migrate to **GPT-5.6 Terra/Luna**; v0.144.6 corrected Sol/Terra/Luna context windows to **272,000 tokens** and refreshed bundled instructions (see Available Models). Changelog-only: contextual conversation branching when editing an earlier prompt or retrying a safety-buffered turn; MCP reliability (startup timeouts, non-blocking OAuth discovery, serialized token refreshes, tool-catalog reuse); Windows native exec-server sandboxing, network-proxy enforcement, hidden helper consoles, quoted hook commands; approval refinements (better forced-`rm` detection, consistent full-access confirmation, rejection reasons preserved); TUI secure clickable inline visualization links, incremental Markdown rendering, ripgrep 15.2.0. Note: `developers.openai.com/codex/changelog` now 308-redirects to `learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog` — older citations resolve through the redirect. Source: [openai/codex releases](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.145.0). | [111](#fn:193) [112](#fn:194) |  |
| 2026-07-16 | Guide v2.44: CLI **v0.144.5** (July 16, stable patch line; v0.145.0 remains alpha — not tracked). **Sandbox/approvals:** dangerous-command detection recognizes more forced `rm` forms and returns clearer rejection reasons (see Approval Policy). **Multi-agent (retroactive documentation, shipped v0.138.0):** parent-to-sub-agent task text in multi-agent v2 is **encrypted end-to-end through the Responses API** — `spawn_agent`/`send_message`/`followup_task` payloads no longer appear in plaintext in local session logs; custom-provider models not configured for encrypted tool use fail with a 400; Codex-generated completion notifications remain plaintext as typed `agent_message` items; the audit-trail regression issue remains open (see Multi-Agent). v0.144.4 had no user-facing changes. Source: [openai/codex releases](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.144.5), [PR #26210](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26210). | [108](#fn:190) [109](#fn:191) [110](#fn:192) |  |
| 2026-07-09 | Guide v2.43: CLI **v0.144.0** (July 9, promoted from the alpha line). **Approvals:** new **`writes` app-approval mode** — declared read-only app actions run free, writes prompt (see App Approval Mode). **MCP:** tools request authentication **interactively without an experimental opt-in** (see MCP section). **`/usage`:** reset credits show type + expiration with a redemption picker (see slash-command table). Changelog-only: selecting Ultra reasoning warns when high multi-agent concurrency could spike usage; app-server hosts can provide auth at runtime and redirect logins to a hosted page; device-code login warnings explain phishing recognition; Bedrock model names clearly identify GPT-5.6 family/variant; resumed ChatGPT threads recover when compaction references a retired model; Windows sandbox write/delete fixes; `/review` branch picker faster in large repos. Source: [openai/codex releases](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.144.0). | [107](#fn:189) |  |
| 2026-07-08 | Guide v2.42: CLI **v0.143.0** (July 8, promoted from the v0.143.0-alpha line, superseding the v0.142.x patch line). **Plugins:** remote plugins are now **enabled by default** with npm marketplace sources and visible remote/local versions (see Plugins). **Config/proxy:** system-proxy auth now extends to **Windows** and to Responses API traffic, with PAC/WPAD autoconfiguration (see Proxy Support). **Remote control:** new **`codex remote-control pair`** generates a manual pairing code for out-of-band controllers (see `codex remote-control`). **Models:** Amazon Bedrock adds **GPT-5.6 Sol/Terra/Luna** with `max` reasoning effort (see Available Models). **App-server:** clients can inspect environments, list descendant threads, and fork history through a turn (see App-Server Thread Pagination). Changelog-only: Windows ConPTY input fixes, exec-server offline recovery, installer rate-limit resilience, security dependency bumps (OpenSSL/Hono/fast-uri/quick-xml/crossbeam-epoch). (MCP tool-search-by-default was already documented from the alpha line.) Source: [openai/codex releases](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.143.0). | [106](#fn:188) |  |
| 2026-07-01 | Guide v2.41: CLI v0.142.2–v0.142.5 (stable patch line; v0.143.0 remains alpha — not tracked). **MCP:** tools now use **tool search by default when supported** — on-demand discovery instead of upfront loading, compatible with older models/providers; remote stdio MCP servers accept absolute working directories in the remote platform’s path format (see MCP section). **Security:** PowerShell commands containing executable AST regions the safety classifier cannot inspect now **require approval** (see Approval Policy); v0.142.5 stops full Responses WebSocket request payloads from being written to trace logs. **Config:** `respect_system_proxy` lets macOS auth clients honor system proxy/PAC/WPAD settings (see Proxy Support). Changelog-only: plugins support dark-mode logos in manifests and catalogs; remote catalogs return curated featured rankings; expired Amazon Bedrock credentials produce actionable recovery guidance; remote HTTP(S) image inputs return clear model-visible validation errors; Code Mode warns when the selected model lacks required metadata; bundled OpenSSL/esbuild updated. v0.142.3/v0.142.4 were maintenance-only. **Also this update: title/description rescued to the evergreen CTR-audit form (title lock).** Source: [openai/codex releases](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases). | [105](#fn:187) |  |
| 2026-06-23 | Guide v2.40: CLI v0.142.0 stable (June 22, promoted from the v0.142.0-alpha line). **`/usage` credits:** `/usage` now shows and redeems earned usage-limit reset credits, with confirmation, retry, and refreshed availability states. **`/plugins` reorganized:** remote plugins group into **OpenAI Curated**, **Workspace**, and **Shared with me** sections, and eligible turns can recommend and install relevant plugins. **Rollout token budgets:** configurable token budgets track usage across agent threads, surface remaining-budget reminders, and abort turns when exhausted. **Multi-agent delegation modes:** app-server clients can configure delegation as `disabled`, `explicit-request-only`, or `proactive` at the thread and turn level. **Indexed web search:** a new indexed web-search mode permits live searches while restricting direct page access to server-approved URLs. **Time:** Codex can receive scheduled UTC time reminders and query the current time directly, including via client-provided app-server clocks. Fixes: Linux TUI rendering after Ctrl+Z suspend/`fg` resume; exec-server process and stdio MCP session reconnection resilience; remote-environment path preservation across operating systems; plugin loading, installation, and manifest handling; parent-agent visibility into subagent errors; goal-first thread persistence in `thread/list` and `thread/search`. (Latest pre-release is v0.143.0-alpha.x as of June 23, still alpha — not tracked.) Source: [openai/codex releases](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.142.0) and [Codex Changelog](https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog). | [104](#fn:186) |  |
| 2026-06-18 | Guide v2.39: CLI v0.141.0 stable (June 18, promoted from the v0.141.0-alpha line). **Encrypted remote executors:** remote executors now use authenticated, end-to-end encrypted **Noise-relay channels**, and TLS accepts **P-521 certificate signatures** for enterprise-proxy compatibility. **Cross-platform remote execution** preserves the executor’s native working directory and shell. **Windows sandbox:** execution improvements including automatic credential recovery. **Performance:** large tool-heavy sessions cache tool search to cut latency and memory, and prompt-image caching is bounded to 64 MiB. **TUI:** input prompts can auto-resolve after inactivity with a countdown timer; realtime clients gain speech-append control. (Latest pre-release is v0.142.0-alpha.x as of June 19, still alpha — not tracked.) Source: [openai/codex releases](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.141.0) and [Codex Changelog](https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog). | [103](#fn:185) |  |
| 2026-06-16 | Guide v2.38: CLI v0.140.0 stable (June 15, promoted from the v0.140.0-alpha line). **`/usage`:** new views for daily, weekly, and cumulative account token activity. **Session deletion:** `codex delete`, `/delete`, and app-server `thread/delete` permanently remove a session with confirmation safeguards. **`/import`:** selectively import setup, project configuration, and recent chats from Claude Code. **Unified mentions:** typing `@` opens one menu for files, plugins, and skills by default. **Amazon Bedrock:** managed API-key authentication, plus encrypted local storage for CLI and MCP OAuth credentials. **`/goal`** now preserves oversized text, large pasted blocks, and image attachments in remote app-server sessions. **Removed:** experimental `/realtime` voice controls and audio dependencies dropped from the TUI. Fixes: corrupted SQLite state databases auto-backup and rebuild from rollout data; `/review` no longer crashes when Esc is pressed with queued guidance; MCP reliability via transient-startup retries and disabled-server preservation; remote plugin uninstall + surfacing apps needing auth; persisted “Don’t remind me” update dismissals; non-TTY background commands interruptible with Ctrl-C while preserving output. Maintenance: Git filesystem-monitor preservation and archive-lookup acceleration for large repos. (Latest pre-release is v0.141.0-alpha.x as of June 16, still alpha — not tracked.) Source: [openai/codex releases](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.140.0) and [Codex Changelog](https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog). | [102](#fn:184) |  |
| 2026-06-09 | Guide v2.37: CLI v0.139.0 stable (June 9, promoted from the v0.139.0-alpha line). **Code-mode web search:** code mode can call standalone web search directly (including from nested JavaScript tool calls) and receive plaintext results. **MCP schemas:** tool/connector input schemas now preserve `oneOf`/`allOf` constructs for better large-schema structure preservation and MCP compatibility. **`codex doctor`:** adds editor and pager environment details, redacting sensitive values in JSON output. **Plugins:** `codex plugin marketplace list --json` exposes plugin sources, plus faster cached-catalog plugin listing. Fixes: `codex resume --last` / `codex fork --last` treat trailing args as prompts (not session IDs); subagent MCP startup warnings no longer surface in the wrong thread context; image edits reference exact file paths; tilde URLs linkify fully in the TUI; thread resets (`/new`, `/clear`, `/fork`) preserve cloud-managed requirements/feature flags; sandbox execution consistently preserves approval decisions and enforces proxy-only networking. Maintenance: separate symbol archives with line tables; `rusty_v8` bumped to 149.2.0. (Latest pre-release is v0.140.0-alpha.x as of June 9, still alpha — not tracked.) Source: [openai/codex releases](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.139.0) and [Codex Changelog](https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog). | [116](#fn:183) |  |
| 2026-06-08 | Guide v2.36: CLI v0.138.0 stable (June 8, promoted from the v0.138.0-alpha line). **`/app` desktop handoff** — `/app` hands a running CLI session off to the desktop app on macOS and Windows. **Local image paths exposed to models** — the model can reference local image file paths directly. **More flexible reasoning-effort selection.** **Plugins:** enhanced automation with structured JSON output. Source: [openai/codex releases](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.138.0) and [Codex Changelog](https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog). | [117](#fn:182) |  |
| 2026-06-04 | Guide v2.35: CLI v0.137.0 stable (June 4, promoted from the alpha line first seen June 3). **TUI:** controls support F13–F24 keybindings; searchable menus accept paste; a compact reasoning-only status/title item. **Enterprise/admin:** flows surface monthly credit limits and cloud-managed config bundles. **Remote control:** clients can initiate pairing and manage controller grants. **Plugins:** workflows gain machine-readable JSON output and cached remote catalog suggestions. **Tools:** hosted web and image tools available in more code-mode flows; standalone web searches can run in parallel. **Multi-agent:** v2 runtime improvements with cleaner follow-up handling and metadata defaults. Fixes: prompt cancellation restores draft, attachments, and collaboration mode; macOS app launch and Windows SQLite startup reliability; plugin manifest ordering and deduplication; permission requests honor environment identity. Source: [openai/codex releases](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.137.0) and [Codex Changelog](https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog). | [118](#fn:181) |  |
| 2026-06-02 | Guide v2.34: CLI v0.136.0 stable (June 1). **Session archiving:** `/archive` in the TUI plus `codex archive` / `codex unarchive` CLI commands; an archived session is protected from resume or fork until restored. **TUI markdown:** web links stay clickable via OSC 8 metadata, and cramped tables fall back to readable key/value records without losing link targets. **App-server:** `codex app-server --stdio` launches in stdio mode for editor/host integrations; resumes threads with initial-turns pages; shows richer MCP server status. **Remote/security:** remote execution setup accepts `CODEX_API_KEY` for approved OpenAI hosts; remote-control websockets use short-lived server tokens instead of ChatGPT access tokens; `/diff` is blocked from executing repository-provided Git helpers (command-safety fix); ChatGPT auth refreshes near-expiry tokens and prompts relogin on reused refresh tokens; Bedrock auth falls back to `AWS_REGION`/`AWS_DEFAULT_REGION`. **Windows (alpha):** `codex sandbox setup --elevated` provisioning path for administrators. **Image generation:** feature-gated standalone image-generation extension via the native image-artifact completion pipeline. Note: yesterday’s pass held this at “v0.136.0 alpha only”; it was promoted to stable June 1. Source: [openai/codex releases](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.136.0) and [Codex Changelog](https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog). | [119](#fn:180) |  |
| 2026-05-28 | Guide v2.33: CLI v0.134.0 stable + v0.135.0 release. **v0.134.0 (May 26):** added search across local conversation history with case-insensitive content matches and result previews; made `--profile` the primary profile selector across CLI, TUI permissions, and sandbox flows with legacy profile configs rejected through migration guidance; improved MCP setup with per-server environment targeting and OAuth options for streamable HTTP servers; made connector tool schemas more reliable by preserving local `$ref`/`$defs` and compacting oversized schemas; let read-only MCP tools run concurrently when they advertise `readOnlyHint`; added richer extension/hook context including conversation history for extension tools. Bug fixes: remote reliability (stale exec-server websocket reconnect, remote retry); Windows TUI rendering corruption restored via virtual terminal mode; workspace-specific usage-limit messages for credit and spend-cap failures; shared plugin-level icon assets for skills; active permission profile metadata preserved when syncing auto-review runtime settings; Node-based tools honor Codex’s managed network proxy env. **v0.135.0 (May 28):** `codex doctor` reports richer environment, Git, terminal, app-server, and thread inventory; `/status` shows remote connection details and server version when the TUI is connected over a remote; vim mode gains text-object editing, improved word/line-end behavior, and configurable interrupt-turn; `/permissions` understands named permission profiles and displays custom ones; packaged Codex builds discover and use the bundled patched zsh helper across supported macOS and Linux; Python SDK exposes friendly `Sandbox` presets for thread and turn APIs. Bug fixes: TUI markdown tables and multiline lists render more readably with better column sizing and app-mention handling; TUI output stability on macOS and Zellij (no more stderr/composer corruption or raw-output bleed); slash-command completion preserves draft text for