| 2026-04-24 | Guide v2.21: **GPT-5.5 launch (April 23–24, 2026)** + CLI v0.122.0–v0.125.0. **GPT-5.5** is OpenAI’s new flagship — **400K context window in Codex (1M in the API)**, $5/$30 per MTok input/output (2× the GPT-5.4 rate, but ~20% effective increase after token-efficiency gains). Benchmarks: **82.7% Terminal-Bench 2.0** (SOTA), 84.9% GDPval, 78.7% OSWorld-Verified, 98.0% Tau2-bench Telecom. Available in Codex CLI/web/desktop and the API; recommended default for most Codex tasks. ChatGPT Plus/Pro/Business/Enterprise/Edu/Go rollout April 23; API April 24. **90+ new plugin partners** including Atlassian Rovo, CircleCI, CodeRabbit, GitLab Issues, Microsoft Suite, Neon by Databricks, Remotion, Render, and Superpowers. **CLI v0.122.0**: filesystem deny-read glob policies + managed deny-read requirements + platform sandbox enforcement + isolated `codex exec` runs that ignore user config/rules; tool discovery and image generation enabled by default; higher-detail image handling with original-detail metadata for MCP and `js_repl`; app-server stale-prompt resolution across clients; resumed/forked threads replay token usage immediately; remote-control startup tolerates missing ChatGPT auth; MCP startup cancellation works again through app-server sessions; internal split into `codex-core-plugins`. **CLI v0.123.0**: built-in `amazon-bedrock` model provider with AWS profile support; **`/mcp verbose`** for full MCP diagnostics, resources, and resource templates (plain `/mcp` stays fast); plugin MCP loading accepts both `mcpServers` and top-level server maps in `.mcp.json`; realtime handoffs deliver transcript deltas to background agents (with explicit silent-stay option); host-specific `remote_sandbox_config` for remote environments; refreshed bundled model metadata (gpt-5.4 default at the time). Fixes: `/copy` after rollback, queued text while shell command running, VS Code WSL Unicode/dead-key input, stale proxy env restore, `codex exec` inheriting root-level shared flags, leaked review prompts in TUI. **CLI v0.124.0**: TUI quick reasoning controls (**`Alt+,`** lower / **`Alt+.`** raise); accepted model upgrades reset reasoning to new model’s default; app-server sessions manage **multiple environments** with per-turn environment + working-directory selection; **first-class Amazon Bedrock support** for OpenAI-compatible providers (AWS SigV4 signing, credential auth); remote plugin marketplaces with reliable detail lookups and larger result pages; **hooks are now stable** — configurable inline in `config.toml` and `requirements.toml`, observe MCP tools + `apply_patch` + long-running Bash sessions; **eligible ChatGPT plans default to Fast service tier** unless explicitly opted out. Fixes: Cloudflare cookies preserved across approved ChatGPT hosts, websocket reliability under load, permission-mode drift across side conversations, `wait_agent` mailbox-queue timing, local stdio MCP relative-command path resolution, startup managed-config edge cases. **CLI v0.125.0** (April 24): app-server **Unix socket transport**, pagination-friendly resume/fork, sticky environments, remote thread config/store plumbing; app-server plugin management installs remote plugins and upgrades configured marketplaces; **permission profiles round-trip** across TUI sessions, user turns, MCP sandbox state, shell escalation, and app-server APIs; model providers own model discovery with AWS/Bedrock account state exposed to app clients; **`codex exec --json` reports reasoning-token usage**; rollout tracing records tool/code-mode/session/multi-agent relationships with a debug reducer command. Fixes: `/review` interrupt no longer wedges TUI, exec-server output/stream-closure handling, app-server respects explicitly untrusted project config, websocket disconnection during notification bursts, Windows sandbox startup and background process handling, config-schema validation for thread limits and agent paths. | [83](#fn:160) [84](#fn:161) [85](#fn:162) |  |
