102. [Codex CLI v0.140.0 release notes](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.140.0) and [Codex Changelog (OpenAI Developers)](https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog). Promoted to stable June 15, 2026 (from the v0.140.0-alpha line). New features: `/usage` views for daily, weekly, and cumulative account token activity; `/goal` preserves oversized text, large pasted blocks, and image attachments in remote app-server sessions; session deletion via `codex delete`, `/delete`, and app-server `thread/delete` with confirmation safeguards; `/import` for selectively importing setup, project configuration, and recent chats from Claude Code; typing `@` opens a unified mentions menu for files, plugins, and skills by default; managed Amazon Bedrock API-key authentication and encrypted local storage for CLI and MCP OAuth credentials. Bug fixes: corrupted SQLite state databases auto-backup and rebuild from rollout data; `/review` no longer crashes when Esc is pressed with queued guidance; MCP reliability via transient startup-failure retries and disabled-server preservation; fixed remote plugin uninstall requests and surfaced apps requiring authentication; persisted “Don’t remind me” update dismissals and cleared stale running-hook indicators; non-TTY background commands interruptible with Ctrl-C while preserving output. Performance/maintenance: Git filesystem-monitor preservation and archive-lookup acceleration for large repos; removed experimental `/realtime` voice controls and audio dependencies from the TUI. The latest pre-release as of June 16, 2026 is the `rust-v0.141.0-alpha` line (prerelease) — 0.141.0 is still alpha and is not tracked by this guide, which follows stable. Current-session verification June 16, 2026: GitHub releases and the OpenAI Codex changelog confirm `rust-v0.140.0` as the latest stable. [↩](#fnref:184 "Jump back to footnote 102 in the text")[↩](#fnref2:184 "Jump back to footnote 102 in the text")[↩](#fnref3:184 "Jump back to footnot