103. [Codex CLI v0.141.0 release notes](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.141.0) and [Codex Changelog (OpenAI Developers)](https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog). Promoted to stable June 18, 2026 (from the v0.141.0-alpha line). Security/infrastructure: remote executors use authenticated, end-to-end encrypted Noise-relay channels; TLS supports P-521 certificate signatures for enterprise proxy compatibility. Cross-platform: remote execution preserves executor-native working directories and shells; Windows sandbox execution improvements including automatic credential recovery. Performance: reduced latency and memory in large, tool-heavy sessions by caching tool search; bounded prompt-image caching to 64 MiB. UI: TUI input prompts can auto-resolve after inactivity with a countdown timer; realtime clients gain speech-append control. The latest pre-release as of June 19, 2026 is the `rust-v0.142.0-alpha` line (prerelease) — 0.142.0 is still alpha and not tracked by this guide, which follows stable. Current-session verification June 18, 2026: GitHub releases and the OpenAI Codex changelog confirm `rust-v0.141.0` as the latest stable. [↩](#fnref:185 "Jump back to footnote 103 in the text")[↩](#fnref2:185 "Jump back to footnote 103 in the text")

104. [Codex CLI v0.142.0 release notes](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.142.0) and [Codex Changelog (OpenAI Developers)](https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog). Promoted to stable June 22, 2026 (from the v0.142.0-alpha line). New features: `/usage` can show and redeem earned usage-limit reset credits, with confirmation, retry, and refreshed availability states; `/plugins` organizes remote plugins into OpenAI Curated, Workspace, and Shared with me sections, while eligible turns can recommend and install relevant plugins; configurable rollout token budgets track usage across agent threads, provide remaining-budget reminders, and abort turns when exhausted; app-server clients can configure multi-agent delegation as disabled, explicit-request-only, or proactive at the thread and turn level; an indexed web-search mode permits live searches while restricting direct page access to server-approved URLs; Codex can receive scheduled UTC time reminders and query the current time directly, including through client-provided app-server clocks. Bug fixes: Linux TUI rendering after Ctrl+Z suspend/fg resume; exec-server process and stdio MCP session reconnection resilience; remote-environment path preservation across operating systems; plugin loading, installation, and manifest handling improvements; parent-agent visibility into subagent errors; goal-first thread persistence in `thread/list` and `thread/search`. The latest pre-release as of June 23, 2026 is the `rust-v0.143.0-alpha` line (prerelease) — 0.143.0 is still alpha and not tracked by this guide, which follows stable. Current-session verification June 23, 2026: GitHub releases and the OpenAI Codex changelog confirm `rust-v0.142.0` as the latest stable. [↩](#fnref:186 "Jump back to footnote 104 in the text")[↩](#fnref2:186 "Jump back to footnote 104 in the text")[↩](#fnref3:186 "Jump back to footnote 104 in the text")

